#: ../../source/docs/common-MAVLink-high-latency.rst:5
#: 91f0217bf86c4b48ad3ccbc4737524a1
msgid "MAVLink High Latency Mode"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-MAVLink-high-latency.rst:7
#: e6c472a0b6344d5aa38916e106feb6eb
msgid "ArduPilot supports the `MAVLink High Latency <https://mavlink.io/en/services/high_latency.html>`__ protocol. This designed for very low bandwidth or high cost links, such as satellite or LoRA."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-MAVLink-high-latency.rst:9
#: 1ac7798a20aa400bb2c8096bd9a26f5c
msgid "Within this protocol, only the `HIGH_LATENCY2 <https://mavlink.io/en/messages/common.html#HIGH_LATENCY2>`__ MAVLink message is sent once per 5 seconds. Any responses to MAVLink commands or requests (such as command acknowledgements or parameter requests) will be sent too."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-MAVLink-high-latency.rst:11
#: 456c152d53804ee697d67928d6de40f6
msgid "MAVLink High Latency is available as an option on any telemetry port. A typical use case is to have a standard MAVLink telemetry port for initial configuration and system checkout - usually a radio modem or 4G link. A low-bandwidth modem will be connected on a 2nd telemetry port, which the user can activate"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-MAVLink-high-latency.rst:14
#: 1fc37fe1f788461d9325819f68fbc0ec
msgid "Configuration"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-MAVLink-high-latency.rst:16
#: ff37f9f4ea4142bda155521b8415e872
msgid "Make sure the desired telemetry port protocol is set to option MAVLink High Latency (``SERIALn_PROTOCOL = 43``)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-MAVLink-high-latency.rst:18
#: e156690fe3a34fe08bdd7e6b66889a98
msgid "In MAVProxy use the ``link hl on|off`` to enable or disable sending telemetry on the High Latency port"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-MAVLink-high-latency.rst:20
#: 79034bdc191b493a8e662688a8d04041
msgid "In QGroundControl connect using the ``High Latency`` option to enable sending telemetry on the High Latency port"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-MAVLink-high-latency.rst:22
#: dc06bdc1caca45988ef5f177c37bc630
msgid "In Mission Planner, use ``Actions -> Do Action`` to enable or disable sending telemetry on the High Latency port"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-MAVLink-high-latency.rst:25
#: b71f1ad355c649369d5907dab24d6bfc
msgid "Notes"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-MAVLink-high-latency.rst:27
#: 2cc041c0bc3e42e7b92b66b62aed829a
msgid "MAVLink High Latency will only send very basic, high level information of the vehicle's position and status."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-MAVLink-high-latency.rst:29
#: d38d5ec9bc8b475695d7ec07b34d0b51
msgid "The bandwidth requirements of MAVLink High Latency are very minimal - less than 100 bytes/sec in most cases."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-MAVLink-high-latency.rst:31
#: 441bb9911c4241cf99b6347950fa93af
msgid "The enable/disable of a High Latency link can be sent over any telemetry link and will enable/disable all High Latency links on the vehicle."
msgstr ""
